1
00:00:01,055 --> 00:00:02,502
[BOYD] Previously on From...

2
00:00:02,507 --> 00:00:03,744
[SARA] I hear their voices.

3
00:00:03,749 --> 00:00:06,055
They said it was the
only way to go home.

4
00:00:06,060 --> 00:00:08,369
Sara, just tell me what you did.

5
00:00:08,374 --> 00:00:09,869
[SARA] I left the door open.

6
00:00:10,561 --> 00:00:13,048
Are you living in town or Colony House?

7
00:00:13,053 --> 00:00:14,673
- Town.
- Julie.

8
00:00:15,107 --> 00:00:16,228
Colony House.

9
00:00:16,233 --> 00:00:17,785
Why are you doing this?

10
00:00:17,790 --> 00:00:18,878
[FATIMA] What's wrong?

11
00:00:18,883 --> 00:00:21,673
I think maybe I-I made a mistake.

12
00:00:21,678 --> 00:00:25,464
[FATIMA] Julie, there are
no mistakes, just choices,

13
00:00:25,469 --> 00:00:28,071
and you chose what was right
for you, and that matters.

14
00:00:28,076 --> 00:00:29,095
Come on, try it out!

15
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:30,463
[KENNY] Every single one of these pins

16
00:00:30,467 --> 00:00:32,658
is a different resident who drove in

17
00:00:32,663 --> 00:00:34,099
from a different location.

18
00:00:34,104 --> 00:00:36,884
That is fucking impossible.

19
00:00:36,889 --> 00:00:41,095
I don't just sit around,
accepting the world as it is!

20
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:43,102
- [STATIC HISSES ON RADIO]
- Someone is doing this,

21
00:00:43,107 --> 00:00:45,119
and I'm not gonna rest
until I figure out how!

22
00:00:45,124 --> 00:00:47,260
I wish you had the luxury of grief,

23
00:00:47,265 --> 00:00:48,788
but you don't, Boyd.

24
00:00:48,793 --> 00:00:50,291
These people need you.

25
00:00:50,296 --> 00:00:53,353
You need to be the one
to lead these people home.

26
00:00:53,358 --> 00:00:55,931
'Cause if you don't?
She died for nothing.

27
00:00:55,936 --> 00:00:58,392
What are you doing here?
You promised you'd stay home.

28
00:00:58,397 --> 00:01:00,091
If I didn't show up, they
would have wondered why.

29
00:01:00,095 --> 00:01:02,103
- It'll be okay.
- Sara...

30
00:01:02,108 --> 00:01:03,283
I promise.

31
00:01:03,288 --> 00:01:05,587
Do you wanna help me bring
over the rest of the food?

32
00:01:05,592 --> 00:01:06,985
Yeah!

33
00:01:08,769 --> 00:01:11,728
[JIM] I just feel so... broken.

34
00:01:11,733 --> 00:01:13,619
We're gonna figure it out together.

35
00:01:14,042 --> 00:01:15,260
Don't worry.

36
00:01:15,993 --> 00:01:18,736
- Whatcha got there?
- Sweet potatoes.

37
00:01:19,537 --> 00:01:21,337
Nice family.

38
00:01:22,437 --> 00:01:25,314
[GASPING BREATHS]

39
00:01:26,437 --> 00:01:28,517
_

40
00:01:35,309 --> 00:01:36,615
[ETHAN] Sara!

41
00:01:36,620 --> 00:01:38,320
[BOYD] Hey. Oh! Oh, no, no, no.

42
00:01:38,325 --> 00:01:40,111
Okay, grab her,
grab her arm, grab her arm!

43
00:01:40,116 --> 00:01:41,369
Hold on, hold on!

44
00:01:41,420 --> 00:01:46,420
Synced & corrected by QueenMaddie
www.addic7ed.com

45
00:01:46,444 --> 00:01:50,166
[GOATS BLEATING]

46
00:01:50,410 --> 00:01:52,970
Hey, Alma. Come on.

47
00:01:54,267 --> 00:01:57,736
There you go, Alma,
a fresh batch just for you.

48
00:01:57,741 --> 00:02:00,806
Hey! Make sure you share this time.

49
00:02:01,470 --> 00:02:04,127
Nathan! Nathan!

50
00:02:04,132 --> 00:02:07,005
It's your sister! Something
happened at the diner.

51
00:02:07,139 --> 00:02:09,111
They're taking her to the clinic.

52
00:02:16,344 --> 00:02:18,400
I really am feeling much better.

53
00:02:18,405 --> 00:02:21,595
I still think you should spend
the night for observation, okay?

54
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:22,973
Do I have to?

55
00:02:23,103 --> 00:02:24,363
It's just, with things like this,

56
00:02:24,367 --> 00:02:26,478
it's best not to take
any chances, you know?

57
00:02:27,369 --> 00:02:29,317
I can have someone go get Nathan.

58
00:02:29,322 --> 00:02:30,369
He can stay with you.

59
00:02:30,374 --> 00:02:34,422
No. He worries. If he comes by,

60
00:02:34,427 --> 00:02:38,572
could you... just tell him I'm sleeping.

61
00:02:38,596 --> 00:02:40,195
Yeah, no problem.

62
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:42,486
[DOOR OPENING, CLOSING]

63
00:02:46,076 --> 00:02:48,322
I'll, uh... I'll be right back, okay?

64
00:02:57,861 --> 00:02:59,837
Hey. How's she doing?

65
00:03:00,521 --> 00:03:03,439
I mean, fine, given the circumstances.

66
00:03:03,752 --> 00:03:05,301
Has this happened before?

67
00:03:05,306 --> 00:03:06,900
Well, I mean, not according to Sara.

68
00:03:06,905 --> 00:03:09,822
And unless there's an MRI
machine tucked around somewhere,

69
00:03:09,827 --> 00:03:11,627
there's no way to really
know what's going on.

70
00:03:11,632 --> 00:03:12,673
- Yeah.
- I'm, uh...

71
00:03:12,678 --> 00:03:15,166
I'm gonna keep her overnight
and see if anything changes.

72
00:03:15,814 --> 00:03:17,572
Okay. You sure you're ready for that?

73
00:03:17,577 --> 00:03:20,205
Look, I don't know
how that door got open,

74
00:03:20,335 --> 00:03:22,244
but I'm not gonna let those things

75
00:03:22,249 --> 00:03:23,908
take this place away from me.

76
00:03:24,252 --> 00:03:25,993
They've already taken too much already.

77
00:03:25,998 --> 00:03:28,923
Yeah. They sure have.

78
00:03:29,262 --> 00:03:31,275
Hey, can I ask you a question?

79
00:03:31,917 --> 00:03:35,790
These seizures first,
the Matthews kid, now Sara.

80
00:03:36,449 --> 00:03:37,660
You think it's possible

81
00:03:37,665 --> 00:03:39,870
to have a physical
reaction to this place?

82
00:03:40,329 --> 00:03:42,204
Maybe something you
might normally diagnose

83
00:03:42,209 --> 00:03:44,047
as one thing on the
outside, but here it's...

84
00:03:44,052 --> 00:03:46,924
Look, Boyd, if you asked
me this six months ago,

85
00:03:46,929 --> 00:03:49,360
I would have said anything that
we've seen here was impossible.

86
00:03:49,364 --> 00:03:51,243
But the truth is, I...

87
00:03:52,774 --> 00:03:56,024
Okay, how long has
this been going on for?

88
00:03:57,976 --> 00:03:59,869
Long enough that it's got
me asking stupid questions.

89
00:03:59,873 --> 00:04:01,701
- Boyd...
- I'm fine.

90
00:04:01,847 --> 00:04:04,545
Come by tomorrow. I want
to take a look at it.

91
00:04:04,550 --> 00:04:07,016
No need. I already know what it is.

92
00:04:09,041 --> 00:04:10,735
Nathan's here.

93
00:04:10,832 --> 00:04:12,961
[SIGHING] She doesn't want to see him.

94
00:04:14,649 --> 00:04:16,477
Yeah, I don't... I don't know.

95
00:04:18,458 --> 00:04:20,581
Um, okay. Go take care of your patient.

96
00:04:20,586 --> 00:04:21,836
I got this, okay?

97
00:04:22,243 --> 00:04:24,149
And I'm good.

98
00:04:25,183 --> 00:04:27,653
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Whoa!

99
00:04:27,658 --> 00:04:28,838
Is she okay?

100
00:04:28,843 --> 00:04:31,055
She's fine. She's sleeping.

101
00:04:32,735 --> 00:04:34,071
I wanna see her.

102
00:04:34,076 --> 00:04:35,990
And you will, tomorrow.

103
00:04:35,995 --> 00:04:37,298
Kristi's gonna sit with her tonight

104
00:04:37,302 --> 00:04:38,649
and make sure everything is okay.

105
00:04:38,654 --> 00:04:40,329
No, no. I-I need to see her now, please.

106
00:04:40,334 --> 00:04:41,901
You will. Hey, hey.

107
00:04:42,439 --> 00:04:44,746
Is there anything else going
on that we should know about?

108
00:04:45,782 --> 00:04:48,266
Anything that might help
Kristi figure out what's wrong?

109
00:04:49,509 --> 00:04:50,991
No. I'm just worried, that's all.

110
00:04:50,996 --> 00:04:53,008
She's my little sister.

111
00:04:53,547 --> 00:04:55,915
Right. Look,

112
00:04:57,072 --> 00:05:00,945
this is Kristi's first
night back since... right?

113
00:05:01,701 --> 00:05:02,977
We don't want to be going in there

114
00:05:02,981 --> 00:05:05,882
and making tonight more
stressful than it already is.

115
00:05:06,446 --> 00:05:08,491
Sara's in good hands. Okay?

116
00:05:08,894 --> 00:05:11,113
Go home. Get some sleep.

117
00:05:11,277 --> 00:05:12,800
You'll see her in the morning.

118
00:05:12,931 --> 00:05:14,193
Yeah.

119
00:05:14,479 --> 00:05:15,958
Okay?

120
00:05:32,507 --> 00:05:34,874
Is Sara gonna be okay?

121
00:05:35,703 --> 00:05:37,618
Well, yeah, she's down at the clinic.

122
00:05:37,623 --> 00:05:39,866
They're gonna take good
care of her. Don't worry.

123
00:05:39,871 --> 00:05:41,351
You remember Kristi?

124
00:05:41,874 --> 00:05:43,968
The nice lady who took care of your leg?

125
00:05:44,137 --> 00:05:47,314
She's gonna patch up Sara
the same way she patched you up.

126
00:05:47,961 --> 00:05:50,007
In the meantime,

127
00:05:50,658 --> 00:05:53,749
we are gonna play a little game.

128
00:05:54,304 --> 00:05:55,499
For you.

129
00:05:56,733 --> 00:05:58,741
Well, we said we're gonna
figure it out, right?

130
00:05:58,746 --> 00:06:01,351
Let's figure it out. Follow me.

131
00:06:02,436 --> 00:06:03,622
[EXHALES]

132
00:06:08,882 --> 00:06:10,939
We're gonna do some problem-solving,

133
00:06:10,944 --> 00:06:12,034
and the way you problem solve

134
00:06:12,038 --> 00:06:13,692
is by asking questions.

135
00:06:14,074 --> 00:06:16,366
You ask every question that might apply,

136
00:06:16,371 --> 00:06:19,093
no matter how crazy,
no matter how unlikely.

137
00:06:19,558 --> 00:06:21,851
You put it up on a board,
you get it out in front of you

138
00:06:21,856 --> 00:06:24,084
so that you can identify
everything you know

139
00:06:24,089 --> 00:06:26,091
and everything you don't.

140
00:06:26,850 --> 00:06:28,983
It'll be like telling a story.

141
00:06:28,988 --> 00:06:32,601
Right, buddy? Question number one.

142
00:06:35,095 --> 00:06:36,530
[ETHAN] Dad!

143
00:06:36,535 --> 00:06:39,585
What? You never wanted
to write on a wall?

144
00:06:46,109 --> 00:06:49,239
_

145
00:06:49,244 --> 00:06:52,726
There. That's where we begin.

146
