164
00:08:28,699 --> 00:08:31,918
♪ "Que sera, sera" ♪

165
00:08:32,690 --> 00:08:36,980
♪ "Whatever will be, will be" ♪

166
00:08:37,657 --> 00:08:41,918
♪ "The future's not ours to see" ♪

167
00:08:42,357 --> 00:08:45,558
♪ "Que sera, sera" ♪

168
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:50,457
♪ "What will be, will be" ♪

169
00:08:52,133 --> 00:08:55,355
♪ "Que sera, sera" ♪

170
00:09:10,190 --> 00:09:14,934
[CRICKETS CHIRPING]

171
00:09:32,792 --> 00:09:36,796
[GASPING BREATHS]

172
00:09:37,488 --> 00:09:38,636
_

173
00:09:39,301 --> 00:09:40,301
Hey.

174
00:09:42,699 --> 00:09:44,269
I can't sleep.

175
00:09:44,503 --> 00:09:48,941
Uh, yeah, me neither. I thought
you'd like some tea?

176
00:09:49,325 --> 00:09:51,066
Do you want some?

177
00:09:52,739 --> 00:09:53,739
Sure.

178
00:10:01,277 --> 00:10:03,754
You and Kenny make a really cute couple.

179
00:10:03,759 --> 00:10:06,523
Oh, uh, no, we're just...

180
00:10:06,528 --> 00:10:07,878
We're just friends.

181
00:10:08,567 --> 00:10:09,701
Why?

182
00:10:09,832 --> 00:10:12,863
He's really sweet, and he loves you.

183
00:10:13,511 --> 00:10:15,316
It's complicated.

184
00:10:15,527 --> 00:10:16,832
How?

185
00:10:16,837 --> 00:10:19,753
Well, 'cause I... [SIGHING]

186
00:10:21,160 --> 00:10:22,918
have somebody at home.

187
00:10:22,923 --> 00:10:28,308
At least I think
she's... still... waiting.

188
00:10:29,552 --> 00:10:31,152
What's her name?

189
00:10:31,829 --> 00:10:33,363
Mariel.

190
00:10:33,917 --> 00:10:36,833
- Were you married?
- Engaged.

191
00:10:37,511 --> 00:10:40,590
I wonder sometimes,
actually all the time, uh,

192
00:10:40,595 --> 00:10:44,925
what it must be like for her,
thinking I, uh, abandoned her.

193
00:10:46,307 --> 00:10:48,590
Um, how about you?

194
00:10:48,595 --> 00:10:50,590
Do you have anybody back at home?

195
00:10:51,661 --> 00:10:53,019
No.

196
00:10:53,744 --> 00:10:55,652
I... I was with someone,

197
00:10:55,657 --> 00:10:59,300
but he wasn't...

198
00:11:00,452 --> 00:11:03,710
It's better that he's
not around anymore.

199
00:11:04,981 --> 00:11:08,289
It's just me and Nathan now.

200
00:11:08,678 --> 00:11:11,124
He's all I've got in the world.

201
00:11:11,716 --> 00:11:15,285
Before we got stuck here, I, um...

202
00:11:16,533 --> 00:11:18,991
Things weren't really very good for me.

203
00:11:20,515 --> 00:11:23,040
Nathan was the one who saved me.

204
00:11:25,428 --> 00:11:27,169
Can I ask you something?

205
00:11:27,300 --> 00:11:28,835
Yeah. Sure.

206
00:11:29,452 --> 00:11:31,913
If there was something you could do,

207
00:11:32,582 --> 00:11:38,543
something that would let
you see Mariel again...

208
00:11:39,334 --> 00:11:43,076
something that would let
everyone here go home,

209
00:11:43,582 --> 00:11:45,770
even if it was something bad,

210
00:11:46,736 --> 00:11:48,172
would you do it?

211
00:11:49,082 --> 00:11:51,474
Wait, what are you talking about?

212
00:11:51,479 --> 00:11:55,832
I wonder sometimes... about this place,

213
00:11:56,347 --> 00:11:58,317
what it means...

214
00:11:59,559 --> 00:12:02,418
why we're here.

215
00:12:03,168 --> 00:12:06,781
If someone came up to
you right now and said,

216
00:12:07,106 --> 00:12:10,256
"Do this one bad thing

217
00:12:10,903 --> 00:12:13,215
and everyone gets to go home,"

218
00:12:14,347 --> 00:12:15,856
would you do it?

219
00:12:17,231 --> 00:12:18,856
Well, we're...

220
00:12:19,652 --> 00:12:22,133
we're speaking hypothetically, right?

221
00:12:22,740 --> 00:12:25,706
- Yeah. Of course.
- Okay.

222
00:12:25,711 --> 00:12:27,234
[CHUCKLES] Okay.

223
00:12:27,614 --> 00:12:28,745
Uh...

224
00:12:30,999 --> 00:12:32,957
I mean...

225
00:12:35,566 --> 00:12:36,902
Yeah, I'd, um...

226
00:12:36,907 --> 00:12:39,153
I'd do anything to see her again and...

227
00:12:39,995 --> 00:12:41,551
And hey, I mean,

228
00:12:41,556 --> 00:12:43,436
if that meant everybody
else got to go home too,

229
00:12:43,441 --> 00:12:46,814
then, I think that's a lot of good

230
00:12:46,819 --> 00:12:49,942
for one bad thing.

231
00:12:52,782 --> 00:12:54,000
Yeah.

232
00:13:01,957 --> 00:13:03,191
Hmm.

233
00:13:03,196 --> 00:13:05,536
[EXHALES]

234
00:13:05,541 --> 00:13:07,021
Tell me you figured it out.

235
00:13:07,486 --> 00:13:09,445
Oh, I-I did.

236
00:13:09,668 --> 00:13:11,598
And the answer is 12.

237
00:13:13,239 --> 00:13:14,886
[CHUCKLES] Okay.

238
00:13:14,899 --> 00:13:17,553
All right, let's go over this again.

239
00:13:20,017 --> 00:13:22,957
Everyone enters from
different parts of the country,

240
00:13:23,580 --> 00:13:25,887
on different roads, in different places,

241
00:13:26,595 --> 00:13:29,378
and they all, presumably,
see the same tree,

242
00:13:29,383 --> 00:13:30,473
same crows.

243
00:13:30,478 --> 00:13:32,088
Jim, Jim...

244
00:13:32,093 --> 00:13:36,754
everyone here has asked the same
question over and over again.

245
00:13:37,332 --> 00:13:39,411
How does writing them on the wall

246
00:13:39,416 --> 00:13:40,614
going to make any difference?

247
00:13:40,619 --> 00:13:42,882
Because...

248
00:13:43,209 --> 00:13:45,778
There are plenty of things in
the world that don't make sense.

249
00:13:45,783 --> 00:13:46,958
Yeah.

250
00:13:47,141 --> 00:13:49,186
Something here is missing.

251
00:13:50,204 --> 00:13:52,278
We just can't see it yet.

252
00:13:53,124 --> 00:13:54,577
But we will.

253
00:13:54,817 --> 00:13:56,997
Well, there's a question
we haven't asked.

254
00:14:09,896 --> 00:14:11,420
No.

255
00:14:12,090 --> 00:14:13,778
Why not?

256
00:14:14,885 --> 00:14:18,019
Because it's crazy. [SIGHING]

257
00:14:21,908 --> 00:14:23,779
I don't want to know the answer.

258
00:14:30,593 --> 00:14:33,168
You sure you're not hungry?
I was gonna make some oatmeal.

259
00:14:33,173 --> 00:14:34,565
I'm not really hungry.

260
00:14:35,053 --> 00:14:36,575
Thank you for last night, though.

261
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:39,184
It's been a long time since
I've had a girls' night.

262
00:14:39,189 --> 00:14:40,928
Yeah, uh, me too.

263
00:14:41,427 --> 00:14:43,757
I mean, hey, no need to
wait for a medical emergency

264
00:14:43,762 --> 00:14:46,215
if you ever wanna do it again.

265
00:14:47,426 --> 00:14:49,080
Oh, your brother's back.

266
00:14:49,719 --> 00:14:52,635
Uh, he's very persistent.

267
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:54,528
Yeah, he is.

268
00:14:55,304 --> 00:14:56,870
Are you... are you sure you're okay?

269
00:14:56,875 --> 00:15:00,273
Yeah, yeah, it's fine.
He just... he cares a lot.

270
00:15:00,278 --> 00:15:01,957
- Yeah.
- I'll see you later.

271
00:15:04,615 --> 00:15:06,379
You're up bright and early.

272
00:15:06,862 --> 00:15:08,477
Sara, we need to talk.

273
00:15:08,482 --> 00:15:09,614
About what?

274
00:15:11,343 --> 00:15:14,804
I'm so sorry I worried
you. I didn't mean to.

275
00:15:14,809 --> 00:15:16,877
It's fine. I just need
to know what happened.

276
00:15:17,007 --> 00:15:18,661
I was just...

277
00:15:19,106 --> 00:15:21,387
I was standing in the diner one minute

278
00:15:21,392 --> 00:15:22,839
and the next, I was on the floor.

279
00:15:22,844 --> 00:15:24,803
I don't really remember
much other than that.

280
00:15:24,808 --> 00:15:26,843
Why are you suddenly acting
like everything's okay?

281
00:15:26,848 --> 00:15:27,927
I need to get to the diner.

282
00:15:27,931 --> 00:15:29,215
Mrs. Liu is gonna be worried.

283
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:30,352
Sara!

284
00:15:30,803 --> 00:15:33,215
I'm okay, I promise.

285
00:15:33,508 --> 00:15:35,372
I love you so much.

286
00:15:44,850 --> 00:15:46,840
Knock, knock. You awake in there?

287
00:15:47,995 --> 00:15:49,520
Yeah, come on in.

288
00:15:49,915 --> 00:15:51,356
Whatcha doing?

289
00:15:52,483 --> 00:15:54,161
I'm making a list.

290
00:15:54,504 --> 00:15:56,259
Of?

291
00:15:56,656 --> 00:15:57,787
All the people that are probably

292
00:15:57,791 --> 00:15:59,314
wondering where we are right now.

293
00:15:59,790 --> 00:16:01,139
Oh.

294
00:16:01,144 --> 00:16:03,234
I mean, it's gotta be
worse for them, right?

295
00:16:04,004 --> 00:16:05,844
Not knowing.

296
00:16:05,895 --> 00:16:07,454
Just...

297
00:16:10,402 --> 00:16:12,418
I made one too.

298
00:16:14,230 --> 00:16:16,981
Pretty sure everybody here
did at one time or another.

299
00:16:20,018 --> 00:16:21,976
Who's on yours?

300
00:16:23,883 --> 00:16:27,408
My grandparents and my friends.

301
00:16:29,993 --> 00:16:31,386
Boyfriend?

302
00:16:31,645 --> 00:16:32,914
No.

303
00:16:33,028 --> 00:16:34,137
Girlfriend?

304
00:16:34,142 --> 00:16:37,293
No, there's nobody like that.

305
00:16:38,948 --> 00:16:41,215
I guess that's a good
thing though, right?

306
00:16:41,220 --> 00:16:43,762
Just one less person sitting
around losing their minds,

307
00:16:43,767 --> 00:16:45,595
wondering where you are.

308
00:16:47,309 --> 00:16:49,335
[EXHALES] Okay. That's enough of that.

309
00:16:49,340 --> 00:16:51,667
We need some fun, stat.

310
00:16:51,672 --> 00:16:53,707
Get dressed and meet
me downstairs in five?

311
00:16:53,712 --> 00:16:54,931
Why?

312
00:16:55,020 --> 00:16:56,020
You'll see.

313
00:16:57,129 --> 00:16:58,848
[SIGHS]

314
00:16:58,853 --> 00:17:02,509
[METALLIC CLANKING]

315
00:17:04,723 --> 00:17:05,768
Hey.

316
00:17:05,773 --> 00:17:07,129
Hey.

317
00:17:07,134 --> 00:17:09,364
No more work this morning.

318
00:17:09,851 --> 00:17:12,356
She's, uh, making the list.

319
00:17:16,427 --> 00:17:18,603
I think it's time we show
her the Brundles.

320
00:17:22,911 --> 00:17:24,788
Just a fucking idiot.
That's special relativity.

321
00:17:24,792 --> 00:17:26,794
Uh... Klein.

322
00:17:27,340 --> 00:17:30,270
Hardy's. Klein. Hardy's.

323
00:17:33,018 --> 00:17:34,667
Einstein-Podolsky-Rosen.

324
00:17:34,672 --> 00:17:36,369
[TRUDY] Where are you going with that?

325
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:40,499
Sorry?

326
00:17:40,630 --> 00:17:42,849
Is that a radio?

327
00:17:43,122 --> 00:17:46,434
Uh... yeah. Sort of.

328
00:17:46,439 --> 00:17:48,582
Why are you carrying it around?

329
00:17:52,004 --> 00:17:54,364
[SIGHING] Because it helps me think.

330
00:17:55,107 --> 00:17:56,123
I'm sorry, I...

331
00:17:56,128 --> 00:17:57,738
You're even cuter when you're awake.

332
00:17:57,994 --> 00:17:59,301
Excuse me?

333
00:17:59,306 --> 00:18:01,308
I watched you when you were sleeping.

334
00:18:01,912 --> 00:18:03,087
I'm Trudy.

335
00:18:03,747 --> 00:18:05,254
Okay.

336
00:18:06,490 --> 00:18:08,318
Too bad you chose the town.

337
00:18:09,516 --> 00:18:14,254
I would've rode you
like an alabaster dragon.

338
00:18:16,245 --> 00:18:17,333
Bye!

339
00:18:32,725 --> 00:18:34,242
[DOOR OPENING]

340
00:18:34,247 --> 00:18:35,515
Morning, Sheriff.

341
00:18:35,520 --> 00:18:38,784
I stopped by the diner, let
my mom know that Sara was okay,

342
00:18:39,020 --> 00:18:40,607
and she made those bread
things that you like,

343
00:18:40,611 --> 00:18:42,903
so I picked up a couple of those.

344
00:18:44,079 --> 00:18:46,560
Uh, Sheriff?

345
00:18:49,643 --> 00:18:52,254
I'm gonna need you to hold
down the fort for a bit.

346
00:18:53,010 --> 00:18:54,801
Is everything okay?

347
00:18:55,898 --> 00:18:57,301
Everything's fine.

348
00:18:58,747 --> 00:19:00,575
I'm gonna visit my wife.

349
00:19:01,292 --> 00:19:02,641
It's been a while.

350
00:19:06,846 --> 00:19:07,934
Okay?

351
00:19:07,939 --> 00:19:09,528
Yeah, sure.

352
00:19:14,810 --> 00:19:17,813
[DOOR OPENING, CLOSING]

353
00:19:17,818 --> 00:19:19,476
[JADE] What the hell?

354
00:19:19,481 --> 00:19:22,207
You guys built a bar
in this fucking place?

355
00:19:22,212 --> 00:19:23,906
Yeah. You end up in a place like this,

356
00:19:23,911 --> 00:19:26,175
you ask yourself, what
do the people need?

357
00:19:26,692 --> 00:19:29,738
Turns out it's not a fucking
gas station, so I figured...

358
00:19:29,743 --> 00:19:33,486
[CHATTERING]

359
00:19:33,491 --> 00:19:34,707
Hey, you okay?

360
00:19:34,712 --> 00:19:36,161
What?

361
00:19:36,558 --> 00:19:38,504
Are... you... okay?

362
00:19:38,509 --> 00:19:41,207
No, no, I'm not... okay.

363
00:19:42,723 --> 00:19:44,481
Are you okay?

364
00:19:44,486 --> 00:19:46,401
Great. Here, drink this.

365
00:19:46,406 --> 00:19:48,061
It'll help you feel better.

366
00:19:48,066 --> 00:19:49,981
What the fuck? How are you...

367
00:19:49,986 --> 00:19:53,288
Why are you all just sitting here?

368
00:19:53,293 --> 00:19:54,899
[GAGS]

369
00:19:54,904 --> 00:19:57,603
Holy fuck! What is this shit?

370
00:19:57,832 --> 00:20:00,692
Just consider it your
poor man's potato vodka.

371
00:20:01,457 --> 00:20:03,418
[GROANS]

372
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:06,548
[GROANS]

373
00:20:08,989 --> 00:20:11,171
You're one of the guys
from the two cars, huh?

374
00:20:11,301 --> 00:20:13,856
[GROANS]

375
00:20:13,861 --> 00:20:16,864
Your, uh, friend,
uh... friend got, uh...

376
00:20:17,950 --> 00:20:19,950
Yeah. Yeah.

377
00:20:20,661 --> 00:20:23,314
Look, if it's any consolation, it...

378
00:20:23,319 --> 00:20:26,051
It gets easier, man, it really does.

379
00:20:27,332 --> 00:20:30,304
Gets easier, that's rich.

380
00:20:30,309 --> 00:20:31,957
That is fucking rich.

381
00:20:33,817 --> 00:20:37,603
You know, you guys are...
You're like rats in a maze,

382
00:20:38,118 --> 00:20:42,427
sitting there, contentedly...

383
00:20:42,736 --> 00:20:44,608
nibbling on your cheese.

384
00:20:48,182 --> 00:20:50,223
This is a paradox.

385
00:20:51,359 --> 00:20:53,578
That's the problem.

386
00:20:54,132 --> 00:20:57,309
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

387
00:20:57,314 --> 00:20:59,793
The immediate question is,
how do we get home, right?

388
00:20:59,798 --> 00:21:03,645
How do we get out?
How do we get out of here?

389
00:21:05,268 --> 00:21:07,749
'Cause unless we know where "here" is,

390
00:21:08,090 --> 00:21:09,185
we can't get outta here.

391
00:21:09,190 --> 00:21:12,063
It's like... it's like...
this, it's like, uh,

392
00:21:12,068 --> 00:21:14,028
hitting a bull's-eye with
your eyes closed, right?

393
00:21:14,033 --> 00:21:15,637
You're just throwing 'em blind!

394
00:21:15,642 --> 00:21:18,238
You don't even fucking know
where the fucking target is!

395
00:21:18,243 --> 00:21:19,979
Maybe it's over here! I don't know!

396
00:21:19,984 --> 00:21:21,255
Maybe it just, like, went that way!

397
00:21:21,259 --> 00:21:23,646
- Whoa, whoa, whoa! Come on!
- [JADE] Throwing it!

398
00:21:24,469 --> 00:21:25,481
Settle down.

399
00:21:25,486 --> 00:21:27,553
Eventually, you just
get tired, you give up.

400
00:21:28,023 --> 00:21:30,834
You accept that you can't just get out,

401
00:21:30,839 --> 00:21:32,115
'cause you have no fucking idea

402
00:21:32,120 --> 00:21:33,249
where you're trying to get out of.

403
00:21:33,253 --> 00:21:37,257
So, you sit around drinking
your acidic potato piss water

404
00:21:37,262 --> 00:21:38,916
that you call vodka.

405
00:21:38,921 --> 00:21:40,009
Yeah.

406
00:21:40,265 --> 00:21:42,318
So, let me guess,

407
00:21:42,323 --> 00:21:44,771
you're gonna be the guy
who figures it all out.

408
00:21:44,776 --> 00:21:46,734
You're goddamn right I am.

409
00:21:46,739 --> 00:21:49,217
People like me, we design the maze,

410
00:21:49,546 --> 00:21:51,959
we place the cheese.

411
00:21:52,457 --> 00:21:54,677
I don't know what you
did before you got here,

412
00:21:54,682 --> 00:21:57,662
but I just sold a company
for an obscene amount of money

413
00:21:57,667 --> 00:22:00,280
based on a quantum computing algorithm

414
00:22:00,285 --> 00:22:02,722
with the potential to...

415
00:22:04,545 --> 00:22:06,242
[SIGHS] I'm not supposed to be here.

416
00:22:06,247 --> 00:22:09,120
I'm supposed to be
celebrating right now at...

417
00:22:11,616 --> 00:22:13,022
Look, the point is we
can't get out of here

418
00:22:13,026 --> 00:22:14,757
unless we know where "here" is.

419
00:22:16,280 --> 00:22:18,299
Right? To solve the paradox,
you gotta understand the paradox.

420
00:22:18,303 --> 00:22:19,710
You gotta identify it.
You gotta frame it.

421
00:22:19,714 --> 00:22:22,543
- Schrodinger's cat.
- What?

422
00:22:22,548 --> 00:22:24,898
Schrodinger's cat,
that... that's the paradox.

423
00:22:24,935 --> 00:22:28,271
You put the cat in the
box and you close the box.

424
00:22:28,276 --> 00:22:29,756
As long as you never open it again...

425
00:22:29,761 --> 00:22:32,240
The cat is theoretically alive
and dead at the same time.

426
00:22:32,245 --> 00:22:34,693
I know what Schrodinger's cat is.

427
00:22:35,286 --> 00:22:38,201
Okay, so, we're the cat.

428
00:22:38,507 --> 00:22:41,467
This place here is the box, right?

429
00:22:42,452 --> 00:22:46,790
So, all those people we
left behind back home?

430
00:22:47,384 --> 00:22:48,768
Well, they're all
sitting around wondering

431
00:22:48,772 --> 00:22:50,774
if we're alive or dead.

432
00:22:51,427 --> 00:22:54,343
So, to them, we're both
things at the same time.

433
00:22:56,992 --> 00:22:59,691
I taught Intro to Philosophy at USC.

434
00:23:00,814 --> 00:23:02,189
Hmm.

435
00:23:02,194 --> 00:23:05,173
Look, uh, I don't know
a fuckin' thing about computers,

436
00:23:05,178 --> 00:23:06,919
I'll be the first to admit that.

437
00:23:07,076 --> 00:23:09,095
But that, uh... that
radio you brought in,

438
00:23:09,100 --> 00:23:11,853
well, if you're so goddamn smart,

439
00:23:11,858 --> 00:23:14,098
why don't you figure out how
to get it broadcasting, huh?

440
00:23:15,204 --> 00:23:16,439
And I'll tell you what,

441
00:23:17,298 --> 00:23:20,478
if the cat turns on the radio,

442
00:23:20,483 --> 00:23:23,837
you can be goddamn sure that
the people outside the box

443
00:23:23,842 --> 00:23:26,366
are at least gonna
know it's still alive.

444
00:23:30,139 --> 00:23:31,915
Huh.

445
00:23:53,829 --> 00:23:55,744
Are you sure this doesn't hurt?

446
00:23:55,923 --> 00:23:58,317
It's just a little sore.

447
00:23:59,311 --> 00:24:00,725
Hm.

448
00:24:01,014 --> 00:24:02,084
What's wrong?

449
00:24:02,089 --> 00:24:04,318
Nothing. It's...

450
00:24:07,494 --> 00:24:09,115
[SIGHING] It's just...

451
00:24:09,120 --> 00:24:11,490
It's just healing so fast.

452
00:24:11,932 --> 00:24:13,803
Is that bad?

453
00:24:14,811 --> 00:24:16,654
No. No.

454
00:24:16,659 --> 00:24:19,052
Um, actually, it's very good.

455
00:24:19,636 --> 00:24:22,076
I think this place is special.

456
00:24:22,383 --> 00:24:25,256
I know it tries to hurt people,

457
00:24:25,386 --> 00:24:28,433
but maybe it tries to help people too.

458
00:24:28,818 --> 00:24:31,553
Maybe that can be one of
the questions on the wall.

459
00:24:32,313 --> 00:24:33,924
What would that be?

460
00:24:33,976 --> 00:24:37,649
Is there anyone trying to help?

461
00:24:37,654 --> 00:24:39,733
[CHUCKLES]

462
00:24:40,527 --> 00:24:42,696
[KISSING NOISE] That's a great question.

463
00:24:42,701 --> 00:24:45,029
[JIM] Ethan! You have a visitor!

464
00:24:45,365 --> 00:24:47,877
Oh. Let's see who that is.

465
00:24:50,055 --> 00:24:51,622
[ETHAN] Sara!

466
00:24:51,627 --> 00:24:53,834
How's my favorite customer?

467
00:24:54,311 --> 00:24:55,895
We drew on the walls.

468
00:24:55,900 --> 00:24:57,529
I see that.

469
00:24:58,550 --> 00:25:00,944
We never draw on the walls at home.

470
00:25:00,949 --> 00:25:02,908
[CHUCKLES]

471
00:25:03,289 --> 00:25:04,733
How are you feeling?

472
00:25:04,738 --> 00:25:06,186
Much better, thank you.

473
00:25:06,191 --> 00:25:09,149
Good. Uh, did Kristi
figure out what happened?

474
00:25:09,154 --> 00:25:11,302
Not yet. It's...

475
00:25:11,533 --> 00:25:13,404
It's just one of those things, I guess.

476
00:25:13,409 --> 00:25:16,029
- [TABITHA] Yeah.
- [ETHAN] There's a playground outside.

477
00:25:16,033 --> 00:25:17,693
Wanna see?

478
00:25:17,698 --> 00:25:19,920
Hey, honey, Sara just
came out of the hospital.

479
00:25:19,925 --> 00:25:22,355
- Sure.
- Okay.

480
00:25:22,360 --> 00:25:25,881
- Yeah. It's okay, really.
- Yeah.

481
00:25:25,886 --> 00:25:27,998
- Come on!
- Be careful.

482
00:25:34,902 --> 00:25:36,904
This one's my favorite.

483
00:26:03,984 --> 00:26:05,422
Hello?

484
00:26:10,143 --> 00:26:11,580
Father Khatri?

485
00:26:19,756 --> 00:26:22,716
[LAUGHING]

486
00:26:22,721 --> 00:26:25,028
[ELLIS] Welcome to the Brundles!

487
00:26:25,033 --> 00:26:26,078
[LAUGHING]

488
00:26:26,458 --> 00:26:28,344
Whoo!

489
00:26:28,887 --> 00:26:30,672
[JULIE] Oh, God!

490
00:26:32,299 --> 00:26:34,214
Oh! [CHUCKLING]

491
00:26:34,603 --> 00:26:36,169
[SIGHING CONTENTEDLY]

492
00:26:37,427 --> 00:26:39,385
See? If you close your eyes

493
00:26:39,390 --> 00:26:40,913
and just listen,

494
00:26:41,476 --> 00:26:44,211
it's almost like being
anywhere else in the world.

495
00:26:44,708 --> 00:26:46,359
How do you do that?

496
00:26:46,945 --> 00:26:48,336
Do what?

497
00:26:49,147 --> 00:26:51,531
How do you act like
this place doesn't...

498
00:26:52,664 --> 00:26:54,359
You're always so positive.

499
00:26:55,602 --> 00:26:58,126
I guess it all just depends on
how you choose to look at it.

500
00:26:59,426 --> 00:27:00,867
What do you mean?

501
00:27:03,002 --> 00:27:07,718
Well, I didn't come to
the U.S. until I was 11.

502
00:27:08,234 --> 00:27:10,764
I grew up in a small village in Iran

503
00:27:10,769 --> 00:27:12,781
with my parents and two older brothers.

504
00:27:13,098 --> 00:27:17,886
My father, he was a
very outspoken cleric,

505
00:27:17,891 --> 00:27:22,104
which wasn't always the most
popular thing to be at the time.

506
00:27:22,892 --> 00:27:25,300
One day, it was my birthday.

507
00:27:25,305 --> 00:27:29,112
Actually, we were getting
ready to go see my uncle.

508
00:27:29,540 --> 00:27:34,065
These men showed up.
They were angry, shouting.

509
00:27:34,250 --> 00:27:36,464
I remember my mother told me to hide.

510
00:27:38,052 --> 00:27:41,511
But I was so confused
because we were just laughing.

511
00:27:42,247 --> 00:27:44,620
My father had told this story about...

512
00:27:48,892 --> 00:27:51,156
He was a really good storyteller.

513
00:27:51,208 --> 00:27:53,964
I think that's what made him
such an effective preacher.

514
00:27:55,005 --> 00:27:58,409
Anyway, I could tell
my mother was afraid.

515
00:27:58,923 --> 00:28:01,581
My brothers had run to the door
and now they were shouting too,

516
00:28:01,586 --> 00:28:05,416
and my mother just kept
saying "Hide, hide."

517
00:28:06,303 --> 00:28:09,436
But I just stood there, I couldn't move,

518
00:28:09,979 --> 00:28:11,714
because it was all so strange.

519
00:28:11,719 --> 00:28:15,722
I mean, we were just
laughing so hard, you know?

520
00:28:16,036 --> 00:28:18,604
It was gonna be the best birthday ever.

521
00:28:18,609 --> 00:28:21,198
The sun was so bright
coming in through the door

522
00:28:21,203 --> 00:28:23,771
that my father became a silhouette

523
00:28:23,776 --> 00:28:25,558
when they dragged him outside.

524
00:28:31,180 --> 00:28:33,417
And then, there was this pop,

525
00:28:35,244 --> 00:28:37,081
like a firecracker,

526
00:28:38,151 --> 00:28:40,414
and the silhouette fell down.

527
00:28:43,217 --> 00:28:44,958
Oh, my God.

528
00:28:47,643 --> 00:28:49,518
The point is,

529
00:28:50,696 --> 00:28:53,433
there are always going to
be monsters in the world.

530
00:28:53,438 --> 00:28:55,310
It doesn't matter where you are.

531
00:28:56,370 --> 00:28:57,604
But I promised myself

532
00:28:57,624 --> 00:29:00,496
I would never let them
scare the life out of me.

533
00:29:01,624 --> 00:29:03,901
- Oh, hey, hi.
- Hi!

534
00:29:03,906 --> 00:29:06,448
Ah, yeah, you just
look too dry. Come here!

535
00:29:06,453 --> 00:29:09,840
Oh, no, no, no! No, no, no, no!

536
00:29:09,845 --> 00:29:11,683
Come on. Yup, we're goin'!

537
00:29:11,688 --> 00:29:14,276
We're goin'! Hey!

538
00:29:14,753 --> 00:29:16,150
[FATIMA] Julie, come on!

539
00:29:16,527 --> 00:29:17,920
Come on!

540
00:29:17,925 --> 00:29:20,551
[METAL SQUEAKING]

541
00:29:23,210 --> 00:29:24,457
That's the most like himself

542
00:29:24,462 --> 00:29:26,378
I've seen Ethan since the accident.

543
00:29:26,383 --> 00:29:28,472
[METAL SQUEAKING]

544
00:29:28,477 --> 00:29:30,479
How long have you lived here?

545
00:29:31,316 --> 00:29:33,052
Just a few months.

546
00:29:33,433 --> 00:29:35,435
Mom and Dad are trying
to figure out where we are

547
00:29:35,440 --> 00:29:37,094
so we can all go home.

548
00:29:37,350 --> 00:29:39,960
That's what the Cromenockle would do.

549
00:29:39,965 --> 00:29:41,528
What's a Cromenockle?

550
00:29:41,971 --> 00:29:43,941
[TABITHA] She's a sweet girl.

551
00:29:47,943 --> 00:29:50,624
Hey, honey. Don't make her sit there.

552
00:29:50,629 --> 00:29:52,012
Those things are filthy.

553
00:29:52,017 --> 00:29:54,996
It's okay. It's...
it's actually kinda fun.

554
00:29:55,213 --> 00:29:58,913
Sara said we can go see
the goats and chickens at the barn.

555
00:29:59,183 --> 00:30:00,183
Really?

556
00:30:00,188 --> 00:30:02,496
My brother, he tends to all
the animals for the town.

557
00:30:02,501 --> 00:30:04,496
I thought it might be fun to show Ethan.

558
00:30:04,501 --> 00:30:06,372
It's just down the street.

559
00:30:06,377 --> 00:30:09,309
Do you want to go?
I'm gonna tell Dad we're going.

560
00:30:09,314 --> 00:30:11,273
[SARA] I can take him.

561
00:30:11,645 --> 00:30:12,729
I don't want to take you guys away

562
00:30:12,733 --> 00:30:14,431
from anything that you're doing.

563
00:30:14,436 --> 00:30:16,525
We're not doing anything. Hey, Jim,

564
00:30:16,530 --> 00:30:18,184
I'll be right back.

565
00:30:18,565 --> 00:30:20,350
Okay.

566
00:30:24,615 --> 00:30:29,402
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

567
00:30:32,768 --> 00:30:34,639
Hey, babe.

568
00:30:36,510 --> 00:30:38,325
It's been a while.

569
00:30:39,456 --> 00:30:41,653
Things have been...

570
00:30:42,398 --> 00:30:45,662
they've been a little
crazy past few days.

571
00:30:46,332 --> 00:30:48,426
Those, uh, things...

572
00:30:49,093 --> 00:30:51,004
they, uh...

573
00:30:52,483 --> 00:30:55,285
they got into the house
where the little girl lived,

574
00:30:56,498 --> 00:30:58,778
got into the clinic.

575
00:31:00,323 --> 00:31:02,614
You know, we were doing
pretty good for a while there,

576
00:31:02,619 --> 00:31:04,099
keeping everything together.

577
00:31:05,003 --> 00:31:07,137
It was almost starting to feel like...

578
00:31:13,160 --> 00:31:14,957
[CLEARS THROAT]

579
00:31:18,043 --> 00:31:19,676
Uh...

580
00:31:20,745 --> 00:31:24,301
I started getting tremors
in my hand a few weeks back,

581
00:31:26,410 --> 00:31:28,145
same way it started with my Dad,

582
00:31:28,150 --> 00:31:30,936
which means the clock
is officially ticking.

583
00:31:31,954 --> 00:31:34,840
But, see, uh...

584
00:31:35,806 --> 00:31:38,731
I have this crazy idea
that might actually work,

585
00:31:38,736 --> 00:31:40,707
and-and if it does,

586
00:31:40,712 --> 00:31:44,933
then I might be able to find
a way to get these people home,

587
00:31:45,957 --> 00:31:47,825
to get Ellis home.

588
00:31:49,898 --> 00:31:54,121
Of course if it doesn't,
if I'm wrong or if I fail,

589
00:31:54,126 --> 00:31:55,707
then, uh...

590
00:31:56,530 --> 00:31:58,610
then I'm leaving these
people in a worse-off position

591
00:31:58,615 --> 00:32:00,395
than they already are.

592
00:32:04,223 --> 00:32:06,184
You were always the one...

593
00:32:07,302 --> 00:32:08,426
[CHUCKLES]

594
00:32:08,431 --> 00:32:10,645
You made all the hard calls.

595
00:32:10,650 --> 00:32:13,035
"Sometimes you got to swing big, baby."

596
00:32:13,040 --> 00:32:15,808
[LAUGHS] 'Member that?

597
00:32:15,813 --> 00:32:17,597
[LAUGHS]

598
00:32:17,852 --> 00:32:20,376
God, you had... [LAUGHS]

599
00:32:21,327 --> 00:32:23,329
[LAUGHS]

600
00:32:25,214 --> 00:32:27,559
[STAMMERS] I do this

601
00:32:28,145 --> 00:32:30,997
Babe, that's about as big
a swing as I can take.

602
00:32:31,002 --> 00:32:32,848
And, um...

603
00:32:33,241 --> 00:32:35,746
And look, I know, I know, I always said

604
00:32:35,751 --> 00:32:40,013
that I don't believe in signs
or any of that stuff, but...

605
00:32:43,043 --> 00:32:45,625
I could really use one right now, okay?

606
00:32:47,509 --> 00:32:49,976
'Cause, babe, I'm standing at the plate,

607
00:32:51,164 --> 00:32:53,875
and I'll swing if you
tell me to swing. I just...

608
00:32:58,813 --> 00:33:00,968
Babe, I just need a little help here.

609
00:33:00,973 --> 00:33:02,453
Come on.

610
00:33:03,465 --> 00:33:05,336
I need a sign.

611
00:33:05,341 --> 00:33:07,212
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

612
00:33:13,014 --> 00:33:14,842
Father Khatri?

613
00:33:17,483 --> 00:33:19,132
Nathan.

614
00:33:20,093 --> 00:33:21,828
Have you come up here much?

615
00:33:22,271 --> 00:33:24,316
No, not really.

616
00:33:24,321 --> 00:33:25,931
It's strange, don't you think?

617
00:33:26,453 --> 00:33:28,367
A place like this...

618
00:33:29,669 --> 00:33:31,789
could exist in a place like this?

619
00:33:35,313 --> 00:33:36,953
Um...

620
00:33:38,271 --> 00:33:42,232
I was wondering, what are the rules?

621
00:33:42,895 --> 00:33:46,398
When it comes to confession,

622
00:33:48,070 --> 00:33:49,609
if I tell you something,

623
00:33:49,614 --> 00:33:52,015
does it stay between the two of us?

624
00:33:52,020 --> 00:33:54,544
Anything you tell me
stays between us and God.

625
00:33:56,545 --> 00:33:58,426
What if it's bad?

626
00:34:01,001 --> 00:34:02,873
What if it's really bad?

627
00:34:04,617 --> 00:34:07,198
- That one's name is Alma.
- Hi, Alma.

628
00:34:07,203 --> 00:34:08,834
[TABITHA CHUCKLES]

629
00:34:08,839 --> 00:34:11,085
Oh, this is so much fun. Thank you.

630
00:34:11,350 --> 00:34:12,773
It's my pleasure.

631
00:34:13,569 --> 00:34:16,137
Really, he's a little sweetheart.

632
00:34:16,868 --> 00:34:18,174
Yeah.

633
00:34:18,618 --> 00:34:20,881
You have a really nice family.

634
00:34:21,489 --> 00:34:23,158
Hmm.

635
00:34:24,688 --> 00:34:27,645
It's okay to be sad, you know?

636
00:34:29,316 --> 00:34:31,317
And it's okay to be afraid.

637
00:34:34,663 --> 00:34:35,965
Yeah, it seems the one thing

638
00:34:35,970 --> 00:34:38,192
that everyone in this town agrees on.

639
00:34:40,778 --> 00:34:42,737
Really, though, you'd be surprised

640
00:34:42,742 --> 00:34:45,267
how quickly all this becomes normal.

641
00:34:49,002 --> 00:34:51,129
I don't want this to become normal.

642
00:34:53,362 --> 00:34:55,407
I just want to go back home.

643
00:34:56,826 --> 00:34:58,239
Me too.

644
00:35:00,273 --> 00:35:02,145
At least we have the talismans, though.

645
00:35:02,588 --> 00:35:04,286
Father Khatri always talks about

646
00:35:04,291 --> 00:35:05,760
how much worse it was for people.

647
00:35:05,765 --> 00:35:08,333
They'd just hide in places after dark,

648
00:35:08,338 --> 00:35:10,371
hoping the monsters wouldn't find them.

649
00:35:11,086 --> 00:35:12,985
Those hiding places are all over town.

650
00:35:12,990 --> 00:35:15,035
It's really good to know about them,

651
00:35:15,040 --> 00:35:17,910
just in case you ever get
stuck outside after dark.

652
00:35:17,915 --> 00:35:19,606
Yeah, I guess.

653
00:35:20,065 --> 00:35:23,202
There's one in the barn.
I can show you where it is.

654
00:35:23,207 --> 00:35:24,736
Really?

655
00:35:24,741 --> 00:35:27,802
Yeah, it's just... It's right inside.

656
00:35:29,441 --> 00:35:30,817
Uh, yeah.

657
00:35:32,644 --> 00:35:35,995
Honey, uh, I'll be right
back, okay? Don't move.

658
00:35:36,181 --> 00:35:37,668
[SARA] This way.

659
00:35:47,839 --> 00:35:51,981
Nathan, you should've
come to me much sooner.

660
00:35:51,986 --> 00:35:54,293
I didn't... Wait, wait.

661
00:35:54,298 --> 00:35:55,489
What's gonna happen to her?

662
00:35:55,494 --> 00:35:57,512
[STAMMERS] I don't want
her to go in the box.

663
00:35:58,129 --> 00:35:59,379
You gave your word.

664
00:35:59,384 --> 00:36:00,879
And I intend to keep it.

665
00:36:00,884 --> 00:36:03,601
But right now, we have to worry
about the people of the town.

666
00:36:03,606 --> 00:36:04,781
She'll be at the diner.

667
00:36:04,786 --> 00:36:07,431
Okay. Come on. Let's go.

668
00:36:35,847 --> 00:36:38,034
People used to spend the night in here?

669
00:36:38,671 --> 00:36:40,362
What are you doing? Sara!

670
00:36:40,367 --> 00:36:42,471
- Sorry, Tabitha.
- [TABITHA] Open up!

671
00:36:42,476 --> 00:36:44,174
I'm sorry. I'm doing this for you.

672
00:36:44,179 --> 00:36:45,604
I'm doing this for all of us.

673
00:36:45,609 --> 00:36:49,052
Why are you sorry?
Just open the door, please!

674
00:36:49,057 --> 00:36:50,648
- I'm sorry.
- [TABITHA] Sara!

675
00:36:51,034 --> 00:36:54,213
Sara! Sara!

676
00:36:57,279 --> 00:36:59,064
Go get your sister.

677
00:37:01,656 --> 00:37:03,179
Father Khatri!

678
00:37:06,881 --> 00:37:09,549
Hey, I've got kind of a
weird question for you.

679
00:37:10,493 --> 00:37:11,948
If, uh...

680
00:37:13,514 --> 00:37:17,112
If someone asked for a sign,

681
00:37:17,956 --> 00:37:21,018
how would they know what
they were looking for?

682
00:37:25,117 --> 00:37:26,466
Sara?

683
00:37:26,597 --> 00:37:27,859
Looking for your sister?

684
00:37:28,476 --> 00:37:29,520
Yeah.

685
00:37:29,901 --> 00:37:31,216
She's not here.

686
00:37:31,221 --> 00:37:32,370
I saw her heading towards the barn

687
00:37:32,374 --> 00:37:33,814
with that Matthews lady and her boy.

688
00:37:35,741 --> 00:37:38,918
[GOATS BLEATING]

689
00:37:38,923 --> 00:37:42,100
[GOATS BLEATING]

690
00:37:49,370 --> 00:37:52,868
[GOATS BLEATING]

691
00:37:55,674 --> 00:37:57,546
Where's my mom?

692
00:37:57,550 --> 00:37:59,552
She'll be right out.

693
00:38:00,668 --> 00:38:02,104
Come here.

694
00:38:03,750 --> 00:38:05,186
I need to tell you something.

695
00:38:06,092 --> 00:38:07,397
Sara!

696
00:38:07,645 --> 00:38:10,221
Ethan! Sara!

697
00:38:11,549 --> 00:38:13,432
I really like you.

698
00:38:13,437 --> 00:38:15,613
And what's about to happen,

699
00:38:16,784 --> 00:38:19,046
it's gonna save everyone,

700
00:38:20,010 --> 00:38:22,463
just like in one of your stories.

701
00:38:23,085 --> 00:38:24,913
You're gonna be the hero.

702
00:38:27,198 --> 00:38:29,177
Where's my Mom? I want my Mom!

703
00:38:29,182 --> 00:38:31,471
- We're doing this for her!
- [NATHAN] Sara!

704
00:38:31,476 --> 00:38:33,920
- Sara, what are you doing?
- This is how we go home.

705
00:38:33,925 --> 00:38:35,100
Let him go.

706
00:38:35,105 --> 00:38:36,713
They told me, this was the last one,

707
00:38:36,718 --> 00:38:38,792
then everyone gets to go home!

708
00:38:39,051 --> 00:38:41,184
Ethan! Sara!

709
00:38:43,307 --> 00:38:44,716
- [GRUNTS]
- [NATHAN] Ethan, run!

710
00:38:44,721 --> 00:38:46,981
[SCREAMS] No! Let me go!

711
00:38:46,986 --> 00:38:49,337
You don't understand!

712
00:38:51,078 --> 00:38:53,776
Oh, my God, Ethan! Ethan!

713
00:38:54,671 --> 00:38:56,325
- [GASPS]
- [SARA] Nathan?

714
00:38:56,608 --> 00:38:57,981
Nathan?

715
00:38:59,356 --> 00:39:00,734
Nathan!

716
00:39:00,739 --> 00:39:01,739
[GASPS]

717
00:39:01,744 --> 00:39:03,707
No!

718
00:39:03,712 --> 00:39:05,652
No, Nathan!

719
00:39:05,657 --> 00:39:07,999
- Nathan.
- [SARA] Nathan, please!

720
00:39:08,004 --> 00:39:09,085
Nathan!

721
00:39:09,090 --> 00:39:11,277
Nathan! Nathan!

722
00:39:13,038 --> 00:39:16,576
Nathan! No! My God, please!

723
00:39:17,397 --> 00:39:19,459
Please, Nath...

724
00:39:26,554 --> 00:39:29,114
You guys are right.
It's not all bad here.

725
00:39:29,467 --> 00:39:31,596
[GIGGLES]

726
00:39:31,905 --> 00:39:33,942
You know, I was thinking, when
we get back to the house...

727
00:39:33,946 --> 00:39:35,905
- [ETHAN] Julie!
- What?

728
00:39:36,198 --> 00:39:38,032
Hey. Ethan?

729
00:39:38,037 --> 00:39:39,140
- [ELLIS] Hey.
- [ETHAN] Julie!

730
00:39:39,144 --> 00:39:40,754
Hey, hey, hey. What's wrong?

731
00:39:40,759 --> 00:39:42,282
- Where's Mom and Dad?
- [CRYING]

732
00:39:42,777 --> 00:39:44,082
Hey, what's wrong?

733
00:39:44,087 --> 00:39:45,687
It's okay. Don't cry.

734
00:39:45,692 --> 00:39:48,782
Come here. Come here.
Come here. It's okay. Shh.

735
00:39:50,624 --> 00:39:52,134
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

736
00:39:52,139 --> 00:39:53,526
Oh, my God! Ethan!

737
00:39:53,531 --> 00:39:54,750
Tabitha!

738
00:39:55,137 --> 00:39:56,137
Ethan!

739
00:39:57,139 --> 00:39:58,836
[TABITHA] Help me!

740
00:39:59,575 --> 00:40:01,751
Please help me!

741
00:40:01,756 --> 00:40:03,072
Help me out here, please!

742
00:40:03,077 --> 00:40:05,229
[JIM] Tabitha! Tabitha!

743
00:40:06,318 --> 00:40:09,194
- Jim! Jim, over here!
- You okay?

744
00:40:09,199 --> 00:40:10,244
Where... where's Ethan?

745
00:40:10,249 --> 00:40:11,256
- What?
- Where's Ethan?!

746
00:40:11,261 --> 00:40:13,132
Go and find him!

747
00:40:13,137 --> 00:40:14,181
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

748
00:40:14,988 --> 00:40:17,736
[JIM] Ethan! Ethan!

749
00:40:17,881 --> 00:40:18,962
Jim!

750
00:40:18,967 --> 00:40:20,298
- [JULIE] Mom!
- Jim, where's Ethan!?

751
00:40:20,302 --> 00:40:21,312
- [JULIE] Dad!
- I don't know.

752
00:40:21,316 --> 00:40:22,569
- Where's Ethan?
- [JULIE] Mom!

753
00:40:22,574 --> 00:40:24,436
Oh, my God! Ethan.

754
00:40:25,176 --> 00:40:26,613
- Oh, my God!
- [ELLIS] Here you go.

755
00:40:26,618 --> 00:40:27,959
Oh, my God!

756
00:40:30,113 --> 00:40:31,680
Come here, come here.

757
00:40:50,524 --> 00:40:54,354
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

758
00:41:04,516 --> 00:41:05,678
- I was too late.
- Hold on.

759
00:41:05,683 --> 00:41:07,039
- I'm sorry.
- Hey.

760
00:41:07,184 --> 00:41:08,881
Jim. Tabitha.

761
00:41:10,662 --> 00:41:12,093
[SIGHING]

762
00:41:12,098 --> 00:41:14,282
- How is he?
- He's fine. He's fine.

763
00:41:14,287 --> 00:41:15,484
- We're gonna go home.
- [JIM] You go on ahead, okay?

764
00:41:15,488 --> 00:41:17,142
- Come on, Jules.
- I'll catch up.

765
00:41:21,102 --> 00:41:22,912
Where is she?

766
00:41:23,764 --> 00:41:27,059
Uh, she, uh...
She ran off into the woods.

767
00:41:27,616 --> 00:41:28,928
And?

768
00:41:28,933 --> 00:41:32,197
And if she comes back before
dark, then we'll handle it.

769
00:41:33,537 --> 00:41:35,428
And if she doesn't?

770
00:41:35,569 --> 00:41:38,287
If she doesn't, then it's handled.

771
00:41:41,054 --> 00:41:42,751
She came into my house.

772
00:41:43,720 --> 00:41:45,635
She played with my kid.

773
00:41:46,334 --> 00:41:47,955
I know.

774
00:41:47,960 --> 00:41:49,343
Look, if there's
anything that we can do...

775
00:41:49,347 --> 00:41:51,088
The fuck is wrong with you people?

776
00:41:51,474 --> 00:41:53,824
You talk like this place
is fucking Mayberry!

777
00:41:54,565 --> 00:41:57,176
One big family, is that what you said?

778
00:41:57,181 --> 00:41:58,879
Are you fucking kidding me?

779
00:42:21,678 --> 00:42:23,375
Where did you find him?

780
00:42:24,189 --> 00:42:27,126
Um, we were just coming back...

781
00:42:27,719 --> 00:42:29,220
Well, it doesn't really matter.

782
00:42:29,225 --> 00:42:32,298
But he was running up the hill
towards the Colony House.

783
00:42:32,303 --> 00:42:34,175
You did good, Julie.

784
00:42:42,438 --> 00:42:44,310
Can you take him upstairs for a minute?

785
00:42:45,188 --> 00:42:46,650
[TABITHA] You wanna go upstairs?

786
00:42:46,691 --> 00:42:47,909
Hmm?

787
00:42:50,191 --> 00:42:51,962
Come on, bug!

788
00:42:51,967 --> 00:42:55,806
Let's go read the "Cromawhatsit."

789
00:42:55,811 --> 00:42:57,157
[ETHAN] It's The Cromenockle.

790
00:42:57,162 --> 00:42:58,478
Oh, yeah, sure.

791
00:42:58,483 --> 00:43:00,829
That's what I said the "Cromawhatsit."

792
00:43:01,283 --> 00:43:03,673
Come on. All right. Just take it slow.

793
00:43:03,678 --> 00:43:05,267
You're good.

794
00:43:06,510 --> 00:43:08,947
Yeah. You got this.

795
00:43:11,995 --> 00:43:13,083
[DOOR CLOSING]

796
00:43:17,308 --> 00:43:19,243
I need something to write with.

797
00:43:27,054 --> 00:43:28,882
[CLEARS THROAT]

798
00:43:29,138 --> 00:43:31,401
Ask every question, right?

799
00:43:31,577 --> 00:43:33,100
That's right.

800
00:43:50,227 --> 00:43:55,293
_

801
00:44:15,450 --> 00:44:17,844
[DOOR CREAKING OPEN]

802
00:44:23,409 --> 00:44:24,680
Mind if I sit?

803
00:44:24,685 --> 00:44:25,686
Yeah.

804
00:44:28,277 --> 00:44:30,584
No. I mean, yeah, you can sit.

805
00:44:30,589 --> 00:44:32,243
I understood.

806
00:44:40,693 --> 00:44:42,956
She just kept asking these questions,

807
00:44:42,961 --> 00:44:44,336
like...

808
00:44:45,444 --> 00:44:47,259
what I would do to go home.

809
00:44:47,443 --> 00:44:48,706
[BOYD] Mm.

810
00:44:51,486 --> 00:44:53,118
I just had... [STAMMERS]

811
00:44:53,123 --> 00:44:55,352
It didn't cross my mind that, um...

812
00:44:55,357 --> 00:44:57,054
Listen. Listen to me.

813
00:45:00,020 --> 00:45:01,587
This is not your fault.

814
00:45:10,352 --> 00:45:12,050
I spent the entire night with her,

815
00:45:12,055 --> 00:45:15,189
and it was just nice to sit and...

816
00:45:16,211 --> 00:45:18,563
talk and... [CHUCKLES]

817
00:45:19,399 --> 00:45:21,421
have a good time, and...

818
00:45:22,231 --> 00:45:25,060
that scalpel she used,
she took it from my clinic.

819
00:45:25,065 --> 00:45:28,498
So, if... it's not my fault,

820
00:45:28,503 --> 00:45:30,999
then who...

821
00:45:32,353 --> 00:45:34,178
Whose is it?

822
00:45:35,941 --> 00:45:38,053
You did not bring us here.

823
00:45:39,460 --> 00:45:42,952
You did not put whatever
thought she had in her head.

824
00:45:44,850 --> 00:45:47,085
You're just trying to
do the best you can.

825
00:45:48,065 --> 00:45:50,589
And a few nights ago, hey, look,

826
00:45:50,594 --> 00:45:53,319
you saved a little boy's life,

827
00:45:55,969 --> 00:45:59,483
and you're gonna save more
lives before this is all done.

828
00:46:00,894 --> 00:46:02,765
Hey, hey.

829
00:46:04,307 --> 00:46:05,961
Look.

830
00:46:07,301 --> 00:46:09,514
I need you to do me a favor.

831
00:46:10,304 --> 00:46:15,265
Cut yourself some slack. Okay?

832
00:46:20,043 --> 00:46:21,914
["IF I HAD A BOAT" BY
LYLE LOVETT PLAYING]

833
00:46:21,919 --> 00:46:23,442
[SOFT GUITAR PLAYING]

834
00:46:24,761 --> 00:46:26,228
I'll be damned.

835
00:46:26,233 --> 00:46:27,930
[SOFT GUITAR PLAYING]

836
00:46:28,996 --> 00:46:30,301
What?

837
00:46:30,306 --> 00:46:31,761
What is it?

838
00:46:32,697 --> 00:46:34,972
♪ I'd go out on the ocean ♪

839
00:46:35,760 --> 00:46:37,674
I just got my sign.

840
00:46:37,679 --> 00:46:40,355
♪ I'd ride him on my boat ♪

841
00:46:40,360 --> 00:46:42,881
♪ And we could all together ♪

842
00:46:42,886 --> 00:46:45,292
♪ Go out on the ocean ♪

843
00:46:45,297 --> 00:46:49,738
♪ I said, me upon my pony on my boat ♪

844
00:46:49,870 --> 00:46:52,870
